{"id":"swh-t0-0001","lang":"swh","tier":0,"domain":1,"text_native":"Habari za leo?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"How are you today?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"How an encounter opens. Greeting before anything else is what makes the rest work.","caution":"Greet before asking. Skipping straight to a question reads as rude even when your language is perfect.","source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Swahili phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Swahili%20phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":"1120852","author":"espamatics","corroborating_sentences":[1120852],"contributor_share":null},"failure_flags":[]}
